{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChU1mb8jH6tzyvQTxntzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4wWgoKexMe4yuGg4yfxZm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nf='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(f).read()\na=\"Nothing is gated on the readings yet (#63).\"\nb=\"Agent jobs are gated on the readings (#63; `limits:` below): at 75% of the 5-hour window (`stop_workers_pct`) no new worker, triage or agent scanner starts and at most one `agent: claude` job runs at a time (the pool's `DeniedSerial` verdict, 5-hour window only); at 90% (`stop_all_pct`) no new agent job starts. The weekly window is paced by elapsed time: `weekly_stop_workers_pct_by_day` has one percent for each of the 7 days of the window, counted from `resets_at` minus 7 days, and on day N new workers, triage and agent scanners stop once weekly usage reaches the N-th value (with no `resets_at`, the last value applies); `weekly_stop_all_pct` is flat. Reviewers may start until the stop-all values. A reading whose reset time has passed is ignored. An Opus limit (the reactive pause) blocks only Opus roles. Deterministic scanners, the merger and roles of other agents are never gated.\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"pr_watch: { pending_timeout: 2h }\"\ni=s.index(a)\ns=s[:i]+\"limits:                            # subscription limits, agent: claude roles only (#63)\\n  stop_workers_pct: 75               # 5h window; at most one agent job above it\\n  stop_all_pct: 90\\n  weekly_stop_workers_pct_by_day: [20, 35, 50, 60, 70, 80, 85]  # 7 ints in 1..100, non-decreasing, each <= weekly_stop_all_pct\\n  weekly_stop_all_pct: 90\\n\"+s[i:]\nopen(f,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngofmt -l internal/config internal/limits internal/pool internal/servecmd; make lint test 2>&1 | grep -v \"INFO\\|WARN\" | tail -20; git -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason"