{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChU2JoK4zHtX7zWFdoVHZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent jobs on `agent: claude` roles are now gated by the 5-hour thresholds, the paced weekly list and the one-job rule. `make lint test` passed except one docs-check test. I fixed that test's cause and reran only that test, which passes; I did not rerun the full suite after the fix.\n\n- **Config:** `limits:` block with the issue's defaults and validation. It rejects a list that isn't 7 values, is out of 1..100, is decreasing or is above `weekly_stop_all_pct`.\n- **Policy:** `Book.Gate` in `internal/limits/policy.go` computes the day of the window from `resets_at` minus 7 days. With no `resets_at` it uses the day-7 value. It ignores a reading whose reset time has passed.\n- **One-job rule:** the pool refuses a second `agent: claude` job above 75% of the 5-hour window. It never touches held jobs, and the weekly window never triggers it.\n- **Gating in serve:** the policy gate is added to the existing reactive pause for `agent: claude` roles. An Opus limit still blocks only Opus roles. Deterministic scanners, the merger and non-claude roles are untouched.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` and the key table in `docs/site/configuration.md`.\n\nI added tests for each \"done when\" item: table tests for the thresholds, the weekly days and a custom list, pool tests for the serial rule, the Opus-only fixture, and config rejection cases.\n\n- **No new loop:** there is no `limits` loop with `Claims() == false` today, and I didn't add one. Gating goes through the pool's existing limit callback plus a new `Annotate` hook.\n- **Hold the PR:** the owner wants to review before merge, and `internal/pool` isn't a protected path, so a maintainer has to hold it by hand.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/239/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,